you  in part one of this video we looked at  the procedures the world has in place  for the event of first contact with  alien life now we're going to get to the  fun part the possible scenarios and  types of extraterrestrial civilizations  let's get right into it most experts  believe that there are two overarching  categories into which all possible alien  civilizations can be placed friendly and  hostile each of these categories can be  further divided into more specific  groups such as friendly or hostile  nomads friendly or hostile  interplanetary refugees and so on let's  start by looking at hostile  extraterrestrial arrival scenarios  before we do it's important to note that  much of the scientific community holds  the opinion that any civilization  advanced enough to travel between star  systems will have no need for violence  and we therefore have little to fear  from alien arrival for the sake of  curiosity  we'll still explore a few possibilities  imagine your favorite alien invasion  movie what do you picture probably  weapons beyond human understanding  usually on a massive scale right there's  a reason that trope has become so  prevalent and it's not just because the  explosions are cool any spacefaring  civilization able to reach earth would  have the ability to harness energy in  ways we've yet to even consider and it  stands to reason that such forms of  energy would be used not only as  propulsion but also as a form of weapon  unlike our science fiction movies depict  scientists believe that any aggressive  alien civilization would be able to  eradicate humanity with little effort  but what would drive intelligent beings  to such acts of aggression it could be  any of several reasons the most likely  being either a need for resources or the  drive to expand and colonize  coincidentally Seth Shostak the SETI  researcher referenced in part 1 of this  video is one of the scientists who  suspects the quest for natural resources  would result in violence he believes  that since there can be assumed to be a  finite amount of natural resources in  the galaxy it stands to reason that  advanced civilizations would fight over  them as we do on earth  of course resources are so abundant in  the universe in different forms and  locations that it does seem rather  far-fetched that a super intelligent  alien civilization would need to resort  to mining earth that being said if such  a civilization did in fact come knocking  on our door there's little we could do  to stop them as for the drive for  colonization and expansion humanity  understands that goal all too well the  history of man is the history of  conquest war for power glory and first  for most the spread of national borders  consider Alexander the Great who at the  age of 20 succeeded his father as king  of Macedon and by the age of 30 had  built one of the largest empires in the  ancient world stretching all the way  from Greece to Northwestern India if a  young man of twenty could conquer such a  huge area imagine what a civilization  thousands of years more advanced than  ours could accomplish colonization often  under the guise of protection or  cultural advancement is intended not  only to gain a foothold in the occupied  territory but also to exploit economic  opportunities and assimilate the natives  into the invaders Imperial culture take  for example the Roman Empire over its  many years of dominance the Roman Empire  colonized large parts of Western Europe  North Africa and West Asia in Africa and  Asia the Romans often moved in and  allowed the civilized inhabitants to  assimilate into the new hybrid Roman  culture while in Europe the Roman Empire  often resorted to using military force  on the disjointed tribes living in their  desired locations strong-arming them  into submission an invasive alien  civilization could easily play the role  of the Roman Empire to such an advanced  species humanity would likely seem  nothing more than cattle to be  shepherded assimilated or eradicated I  will having a foothold on earth molding  humanity into a hybrid human alien  society would allow the intelligent  civilization to effectively claim earth  as their own leave a handful of  enforcers and then continue on their way  to colonize new planets as scary as  these scenarios are it's important to  keep in mind that the majority of  scientists suspect that advanced alien  civilizations will have transcended the  need for violence and will harbor no ill  will towards humanity with that in mind  let's look at the positive scenarios of  alien arrival while it's probably true  that any hyper advanced civilization  could destroy humanity with the push of  a button many scientists and thinkers  suspect that such beings would instead  remember their own violent past and  strive to help humanity avoid  destruction futurist Allen tuff suggests  three approaches a friendly civilization  might use to aid the people of Earth one  intervention only to prevent catastrophe  this approach would involve our alien  friends simply monitoring Earth's  activity and stepping and only when  disaster is inevitable such as in the  case of an all-out nuclear war or an  asteroid collision to advise and action  with consent this approach would be more  hands on or tentacles on or whatever the  case may be it would involve the  extraterrestrials advising world leaders  and acting  their consent to prevent danger three  forcible corrective actions this would  be the most intrusive method and would  involve the extraterrestrials compelling  humanity to take steps to reduce major  risks against our will intending to help  humans advance to the next stage of  civilization  according to tough option to advice an  action with consent is far more likely  than forcible corrective action he  believes that while the aliens would  know their methods and practices are  superior to ours it would be detrimental  to interspecies relations to force  humanity to act against its own wishes  others suggest that advanced  civilizations would first instruct  humanity on morality and ethics before  providing us with technology were not  yet prepared to use possibly destroying  ourselves in the process another line of  thought called the zoo hypothesis  suggests that an advanced civilization  may even avoid contact with humanity at  all instead opting to observe us from  afar allowing our fledgling civilization  to develop naturally at its own pace it  proposes that any advanced civilization  will understand that humanity could  suffer a sort of loss of identity if  they were to provide us with galactic  training wheels so to speak and protect  us from danger like an overbearing  parent though the thought of hostile  civilizations is scary it's nice to know  that the majority of experts believe  advanced life forms will be friendly  whether we ever meet them is another  matter entirely  but it sure is comforting to think that  we might have a super intelligent big  brother out there among the stars if  you'd like to learn more about the  theories behind advanced alien  civilizations or the history of  colonization check out the links in the  description if you enjoyed this video  please take a moment to subscribe to my  channel to keep up to date with the  latest content feel free to leave a like  or a dislike as you please and leave a  comment down below with how you think we  would interact with alien civilizations  you can watch part 1 of this video by  clicking here or watch all of my videos  by clicking here thanks for watching and  I'll see you in the next video

